window.docContents[240].resolve({"/Theorems/#section-tur-n-s-theorem-stability-and-asymptotics":{"contents":"Extremal graph theory asks how many edges a graph on n vertices can have while\navoiding a given subgraph. The foundational result is Turán's theorem, which\nanswers this question when the forbidden subgraph is a complete graph. Recall from\nCliques that G.CliqueFree (r + 1) says that G has no\nclique of size r + 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Theorems","header":"13.2. Turán's Theorem, Stability and Asymptotics","id":"/Theorems/#section-tur-n-s-theorem-stability-and-asymptotics"}});